# Procedural generation

## Existing patterns

- **ProceduralTerrain**: Single-mesh Perlin-noise heightfield; used for fixed arenas (e.g. Creature/Tribal stage terrain). See Scripts/World/ProceduralTerrain.cs.
- **GalaxyGenerator**: Seed-based procedural galaxy (stars, systems, planets); deterministic. See Stages/Space.
- **ProceduralMeshFactory / ModelFactory**: Runtime mesh and model generation for cells, trees, rocks, buildings, etc. See Utils/.

## Chunk-based world

- For large or “infinite” terrain, use a chunked generator: dictionary of chunks keyed by Vector2Int (chunk coord), generate/unload by player position and view distance.
- Per-chunk height from Perlin (e.g. `Mathf.PerlinNoise(x * scale, z * scale) * heightScale`); use a consistent seed for reproducibility.
- Chunk size and view distance are tunable (e.g. 32x32 units, view 3–5 chunks).
- Keep ProceduralTerrain for single-mesh stages; use ChunkedWorldGenerator only where infinite or very large terrain is required.

## LOD

- Use existing CreateLODGroups editor tool for imported models with _LOD0/_LOD1 naming.
- For procedural meshes, reduce vertex count or swap mesh at distance in a custom system; align with project LOD strategy in techContext (e.g. LOD for creatures, terrain, space objects).
